Each urn was chosen with probability $\frac{1}{2}$. From urn A the chance of drawing a red ball is $\frac{3}{5}$, and from urn B it is $\frac{1}{5}$.

So the weight on the pair (urn A and a red ball) is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{3}{5} = \frac{3}{10}$, and the weight on (urn B and a red ball) is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{1}{5} = \frac{1}{10}$. The total weight on a red ball is $\frac{3}{10} + \frac{1}{10} = \frac{2}{5}$.

P(A \mid \text{red}) = \frac{3/10}{2/5} = \frac{3}{4}
